{
  "id": "binocular-suppression",
  "term": "binocular suppression",
  "definition": "Binocular suppression is a method used to present a visual stimulus without conscious awareness by suppressing it from awareness while still allowing its effects on attention or perception to be studied. In this context, it was used to show face images unconsciously and measure how they influenced later performance.",
